Build a macOS SwiftUI Stack app from scratch at ~/Desktop/mac-apps/StackApp with all of the following, in this exact order:

### 1. FOLDER STRUCTURE
mkdir -p ~/Desktop/mac-apps/StackApp/Sources/StackApp

### 2. FILES TO CREATE
- Package.swift (swift-tools-version:6.0, macOS v14, swiftLanguageMode v5)
- Sources/StackApp/main.swift (NSApplication + AppDelegate entry)
- Sources/StackApp/StackModel.swift (StackItem + NamedStack structs)
- Sources/StackApp/ContentView.swift (full app)

### 3. APP FEATURES (all in ContentView.swift)
- Sidebar with search box (filters name + notes, live counter)
- Create named stack (name + notes form)
- Push / Pop values (LIFO, Enter-to-push)
- Visual stack list (top item highlighted, ▲ indicator, UUID prefix)
- Edit stack name + notes (✏️ button + right-click menu)
- Drag-to-reorder stacks (disabled during search)
- Right-click context menu: Rename/Edit, Delete
- Onboarding (3 pages, dots, Back/Next/Skip/Get Started, shows once via @AppStorage)
- Help sheet (⌘⇧/) with Why / How to use / Benefits sections
- Dark mode (System/Light/Dark via toolbar menu, persists via @AppStorage)

### 4. ICON
- Expect user to have downloaded a 1024x1024 PNG to project root
- Ask for filename if not obvious
- Generate .icns via sips + iconutil (all 10 sizes)

### 5. BUILD & BUNDLE
- swift build -c release
- Assemble .app with Contents/MacOS + Contents/Resources + Info.plist
- Bundle ID: com.ikbhal.stackapp, Version 1.0.0
- Ad-hoc codesign (codesign --force --deep --sign -)

### 6. DEPLOY
- cp -r to /Applications/
- Create Desktop alias (symlink or Finder alias)
- Fix Gatekeeper: xattr -cr

### 7. GITHUB
- Create .gitignore (.build/, build/, *.icns, .DS_Store)
- git init, add, commit
- gh repo create StackApp --public --source=. --remote=origin --push

### 8. VERIFY
- open /Applications/StackApp.app
- Report success/failure

Give me ALL shell commands in ONE copy-pasteable block. No Xcode. VS Code + terminal only. Use Swift 6.3.3 / macOS 26.